      "It is worth being precise about what a mirror is, because the usual proxies are crude. A child sees themselves in a book through many things at once: a family shaped like theirs, a flat rather than a house, a grandmother who lives with them, a name that takes two tries for a teacher to say, a food packed for lunch that nobody else has, a religion with days in it that the school calendar ignores.",
