      "The fix for both is quantity and randomness. Enough books, chosen because they are good, that the range stops being a statement and becomes the texture of the shelf.",
      "## Where a digital catalogue helps, and where it does not",
      "The logistics of this used to be the binding constraint. A family in a small town, or a school with a modest budget, could not reasonably assemble a shelf spanning many places, voices and languages. Importing was expensive, and the local shop stocked what the local shop stocked.",
