      "## Which words are worth teaching at all",
      "The list above is a reasonable set of techniques and it skips the question that decides whether any of them are worth doing: which words.",
      "A useful way to sort them is into three tiers. The first is everyday vocabulary — table, run, happy — which children acquire from conversation without instruction. Teaching these is largely wasted effort for a first-language speaker, though not for a child new to the language.",
